@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Data Privacy";
}

<div class="standard-page">
    <section class="standard-page-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Governance</p>
        <h1>Data Privacy</h1>
        <p>Proxy administration records use employee identifiers, assignment windows, and approval permissions.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="standard-card">
        <h2>Proxy data handling</h2>
        <p>Proxy assignments are held in application memory for this sample environment. The data model avoids storing credentials or session secrets in proxy records.</p>

        <dl>
            <dt>Scope</dt>
            <dd>Employee number, employee name, department, proxy window, and leave approval permission.</dd>
            <dt>Retention</dt>
            <dd>Records reset when the application restarts because this sample does not use persistent storage.</dd>
            <dt>Audit readiness</dt>
            <dd>CSV import reports assignment and removal counts, with row-level errors surfaced to administrators.</dd>
        </dl>
    </section>
</div>
